# Cloudflare Pages redirects — src/site/_redirects
#
# Deliberately almost empty. Cloudflare Pages' default routing already gives
# the site's URL policy, in a single hop, with no rules:
#
#   foo.html            -> served at /foo;   /foo.html and /foo/  308 -> /foo
#   foo/index.html      -> served at /foo/;  /foo and /foo/index.html 308 -> /foo/
#
# That matches the canonical tags and sitemap (see generate-sitemap.mjs).
# Do NOT add rules that re-state it (/foo -> /foo.html 200, /foo/ -> /foo 301,
# a /*/ catch-all, ...): layered on top of the defaults they create redirect
# loops. The previous 258-rule file, translated from staticwebapp.config.json,
# looped on /founder, /login, /schedule-demo and every other directory page
# under `wrangler pages dev`, and Pages ignores everything past 100 dynamic
# rules anyway.
#
# Host canonicalization (www -> apex) cannot live here: _redirects accepts
# relative URLs only. It is a Cloudflare Redirect Rule — see
# CLOUDFLARE_MIGRATION.md.
#
# Add a rule only for a page that actually MOVED. Every rule is checked by
# scripts/tests/site-services-positioning.test.ts.

# docs.html and docs/index.html both exist, so Pages would serve /docs and
# /docs/ as two 200 pages. /docs is canonical (its <link rel="canonical">).
/docs/  /docs  301
